# Issue #2 test matrix - Square (S1-S5) and BERT B4, all pinned to MR32_NR7.
# Square goes up to 5000^3 (~750 GFLOP/rep at N_REPS=5) - this group runs with
# skip_ref_run=true and a reduced iteration count in config.json so a full
# scalar reference GEMM and 1000-rep RVV sweep don't take hours on-board.
#
# S3-S5 re-enabled per user request to test the model (B4) and the full square
# family (S1-S5) together in the same run. Previously commented out per the
# issue #7 future-work note (S1-S5's KerGOPs/pack-vs-compute split all land in
# the same narrow band regardless of problem size, see .scratch/issues/0003-*.md)
# to cut board time; that finding was about redundancy, not correctness, so
# S3-S5 are safe to re-run whenever the larger-size data points are wanted.
#
# Row order: BERT (B4) before Square (S1-S5), per user request to run the BERT
# series before the Square matrix. B4 is the only BERT shape pinned to MR32_NR7 --
# B1/B5 are pinned to MR32_NR6 and B2/B3 to MR16_NR15 (see bert_b1_b5.dat /
# bert_b2_b3.dat), each compiling as its own project, so a single global
# B1->B5 canonical order across all three pinnings isn't achievable in one run.
# layer  M      N    K
B4       4096   384   1024
S1       1000   1000  1000
S2       2000   2000  2000
S3       3000   3000  3000
S4       4000   4000  4000
S5       5000   5000  5000
